{"guide":{"questionsToConsider":["Do you want the results to name specific titles, or point to a shelf or reading list you keep updated?","Should the format answer change what you suggest, for example audiobook editions?","Is this for a bookshop, a library, a book club or a classroom, and does the age range need its own question?","Would an extra result for poetry, graphic novels or young adult books suit your readers?"],"howToUseResponses":"The loved book answer is the most useful thing here: read it alongside the mood to make a personal suggestion if someone asks for more. Export the responses to CSV to see which moods are most common and shape displays or reading lists around them. For a library or book club, the topics chosen by nonfiction readers are a good guide for the next themed event.","customizeSteps":["Swap the example titles in each result for books you stock or have on your shelves.","Edit the follow-up question in each mood's branch so it narrows toward the titles you want to suggest.","Share the link on your website, newsletter or a QR code by the till."],"faqs":[{"q":"How do I find a book I'll actually like?","a":"Start with a book you loved and the mood you're in, rather than a genre. Pace and length matter too: a slow, immersive read and a fast thriller suit very different evenings."},{"q":"How does this book quiz decide what to recommend?","a":"The mood question opens a short follow-up for that mood and then leads to one of six results. You can rewrite every result and move the branches."},{"q":"Can a library or bookshop use this quiz?","a":"Yes. Replace the example titles with books on your shelves and share the link or embed the quiz on your website."}]},"doc":{"schemaVersion":9,"title":"What should I read next?","description":"Ask about mood and reading habits, then suggest a genre with titles to try next.","blocks":[{"id":"blk_bookreco00","ref":"welcome","title":"Stuck on what to read next? Answer a few questions and we'll suggest a book to pick up.","required":false,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"buttonLabel":"Start","type":"welcome"},{"id":"blk_bookreco01","ref":"loved_book","title":"What's a book you loved recently?","required":false,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"short_text","unique":false,"minLength":0,"maxLength":150},{"id":"blk_bookreco02","ref":"length","title":"How long do you like a book to be?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_short_something_i","label":"Short, something I can finish in a weekend","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_any_length_is","label":"Any length is fine","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_long_i_want","label":"Long, I want to live in it","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_bookreco03","ref":"format","title":"How do you like to read?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"multi_select","options":[{"id":"opt_print","label":"Print","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_e_reader","label":"E-reader","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_audiobook","label":"Audiobook","image_key":null}],"minSelections":1,"maxSelections":3,"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_bookreco04","ref":"pace","title":"Do you prefer a slow burn or a fast pace?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"opinion_scale","steps":5,"startAt":1,"labelLow":"Slow and immersive","labelHigh":"Can't stop turning pages"},{"id":"blk_bookreco05","ref":"email","title":"Where should we send your reading list?","description":"Optional.","required":false,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"email","unique":false,"businessOnly":false,"allowedDomains":[],"verify":false},{"id":"blk_bookreco06","ref":"mood","title":"What are you in the mood for right now?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_something_gripping_i","label":"Something gripping I can't put down","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_a_story_that","label":"A story that takes me somewhere else entirely","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_something_warm_that","label":"Something warm that makes me smile","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_real_life_true","label":"Real life: true stories and big ideas","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_beautiful_writing_that","label":"Beautiful writing that stays with me","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_bookreco07","ref":"darkness","title":"How dark can it get?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_keep_it_cosy","label":"Keep it cosy, nothing grim","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_tense_is_good","label":"Tense is good, but not too gory","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_dark_and_twisty","label":"Dark and twisty is fine","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_bookreco08","ref":"world","title":"Magic or science?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_magic_and_other","label":"Magic and other worlds","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_science_and_the","label":"Science and the future","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_either_works","label":"Either works","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_bookreco09","ref":"warm_kind","title":"Which sounds more like you?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_laugh_out_loud","label":"Laugh-out-loud funny","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_gentle_and_heartwarming","label":"Gentle and heartwarming","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_a_love_story","label":"A love story","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_bookreco10","ref":"topics","title":"Which topics pull you in?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"multi_select","options":[{"id":"opt_memoir_and_life","label":"Memoir and life stories","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_history","label":"History","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_science_and_nature","label":"Science and nature","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_psychology_and_how","label":"Psychology and how people think","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_true_crime","label":"True crime","image_key":null}],"minSelections":1,"maxSelections":5,"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_bookreco11","ref":"literary_setting","title":"Where would you like the story to be set?","required":false,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_the_past","label":"The past","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_the_present_day","label":"The present day","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_somewhere_slightly_off","label":"Somewhere slightly off from our world","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_anywhere","label":"Anywhere","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false}],"endings":[{"id":"end_bookreco01","ref":"end_thanks","title":"Literary fiction 📖","bodyMd":"You read for the writing and the characters that stay with you. Try Never Let Me Go by Kazuo Ishiguro or Tomorrow, and Tomorrow, and Tomorrow by Gabrielle Zevin.","imageUrl":null,"redirectDelaySec":4,"showSummary":false,"kind":"success","requirements":[]},{"id":"end_bookreco02","ref":"end_thriller","title":"A page-turning thriller 🔪","bodyMd":"You want momentum and a twist you didn't see coming. Try Gone Girl by Gillian Flynn or The Silent Patient by Alex Michaelides: both are hard to put down once they get going.","imageUrl":null,"redirectDelaySec":4,"showSummary":false,"kind":"success","requirements":[]},{"id":"end_bookreco03","ref":"end_cosy_mystery","title":"A cosy mystery 🫖","bodyMd":"All the fun of a whodunnit without the grim parts. Try The Thursday Murder Club by Richard Osman, where four friends in a retirement village take on a real murder case.","imageUrl":null,"redirectDelaySec":4,"showSummary":false,"kind":"success","requirements":[]},{"id":"end_bookreco04","ref":"end_speculative","title":"Fantasy or science fiction 🚀","bodyMd":"You want a whole new world to get lost in. For science, Project Hail Mary by Andy Weir is clever and funny. For magic, The Name of the Wind by Patrick Rothfuss is a long, rich read.","imageUrl":null,"redirectDelaySec":4,"showSummary":false,"kind":"success","requirements":[]},{"id":"end_bookreco05","ref":"end_feelgood","title":"A feel-good novel ☀️","bodyMd":"Warmth and humour it is. A Man Called Ove by Fredrik Backman and The House in the Cerulean Sea by TJ Klune are both funny, kind and quietly moving. If it's romance you're after, Beach Read by Emily Henry is a warm, witty place to start.","imageUrl":null,"redirectDelaySec":4,"showSummary":false,"kind":"success","requirements":[]},{"id":"end_bookreco06","ref":"end_nonfiction","title":"Narrative nonfiction 🧭","bodyMd":"True stories told as well as any novel. Educated by Tara Westover is a gripping memoir, and Sapiens by Yuval Noah Harari is a big-picture read that sparks conversations.","imageUrl":null,"redirectDelaySec":4,"showSummary":false,"kind":"success","requirements":[]}],"endingRules":[],"logic":[{"id":"rl_bookreco01","action_kind":"goto","when":{"op":"and","conditions":[],"groups":[]},"from":"world","target":"end_speculative","targetKind":"ending"},{"id":"rl_bookreco02","action_kind":"goto","when":{"op":"and","conditions":[],"groups":[]},"from":"warm_kind","target":"end_feelgood","targetKind":"ending"},{"id":"rl_bookreco03","action_kind":"goto","when":{"op":"and","conditions":[],"groups":[]},"from":"topics","target":"end_nonfiction","targetKind":"ending"},{"id":"rl_bookreco04","action_kind":"goto","when":{"op":"and","conditions":[{"left":{"kind":"ref","ref":"mood"},"op":"eq","value":"opt_something_gripping_i"}],"groups":[]},"from":"mood","target":"darkness","targetKind":"block","branch":"true"},{"id":"rl_bookreco05","action_kind":"goto","when":{"op":"and","con